  "reason": "The abstract reports on the translation of two cancer vaccine strategies from mice to human clinical trials. For the first strategy (TARP), it states that 74% of subjects had a decreased PSA slope at 1 year compared to their baseline. For the second strategy (HER2), it states that 45% of evaluable patients showed clinical benefit. These represent quantitative measures of success/response in human trials following preclinical animal studies, indicating a form of translational success rate."
